    },
    {
      "text": "Abstract",
      "bbox": [
        283.7579345703125,
        269.91009521484375,
        328.24322509765625,
        280.6578063964844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The capabilities of large language models (LLMs) are widely regarded as relying",
      "bbox": [
        143.5570068359375,
        293.19537353515625,
        468.1295166015625,
        302.1019287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on autoregressive models (ARMs). We challenge this notion by introducing LLaDA,",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        304.1043701171875,
        469.3761291503906,
        313.01092529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a diffusion model trained from scratch under the pre-training and supervised fine-",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        315.01336669921875,
        469.7858581542969,
        323.919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tuning (SFT) paradigm. LLaDA employs a forward data masking process and",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        325.92236328125,
        468.1310119628906,
        334.82891845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a reverse generation process, parameterized by a Transformer to predict masked",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        336.83135986328125,
        468.1309509277344,
        345.7379150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tokens. It provides a principled generative approach for probabilistic inference by",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        347.7413635253906,
        468.48150634765625,
        356.6479187011719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "optimizing a likelihood lower bound. Across extensive benchmarks on general",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        358.6503601074219,
        468.1309814453125,
        367.5569152832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tasks, math, code, and so on, LLaDA demonstrates strong scalability and performs",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        369.5593566894531,
        468.1363525390625,
        378.4659118652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "comparably to our self-constructed ARM baselines. Remarkably, LLaDA 8B is",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        380.4683532714844,
        468.1308898925781,
        389.3749084472656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "competitive with strong LLMs like LLaMA3 8B in in-context learning and, after",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        391.3773498535156,
        468.3023681640625,
        400.2839050292969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SFT, exhibits impressive instruction-following abilities in case studies such as multi-",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        402.2863464355469,
        469.78619384765625,
        411.1929016113281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "turn dialogue. Moreover, LLaDA addresses the reversal curse, surpassing GPT-4o",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        413.19537353515625,
        468.13311767578125,
        422.1019287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in a reversal poem completion task. Our findings show the promise of diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        424.1043701171875,
        468.1308898925781,
        433.01092529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "models for language modeling at scale and challenge the common assumption that",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        435.01336669921875,
        468.1374816894531,
        443.919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "core LLM capabilities discussed above inherently depend on ARMs. Project page",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        445.92236328125,
        468.13409423828125,
        454.82891845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and codes: https://ml-gsai.github.io/LLaDA-demo/.",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        456.83135986328125,
        386.2862243652344,
        465.7976989746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        486.2369079589844,
        113.97760009765625,
        496.984619140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "bbox": [
        125.93280029296875,
        486.2369079589844,
        190.8136749267578,
        496.984619140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Large language models (LLMs) [1] fall entirely within the framework of generative modeling.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        510.1893310546875,
        505.7427062988281,
        519.0958862304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Specifically, LLMs aim to capture the true but unknown language distribution pdata(·) by optimizing",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        520.381103515625,
        503.9989318847656,
        530.8533325195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a model distribution pθ(·) through maximum likelihood estimation, or equivalently KL divergence",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        531.2900390625,
        504.0038757324219,
        541.60888671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "minimization between the two distributions:",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        542.9163818359375,
        283.7103576660156,
        551.8229370117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "max",
      "bbox": [
        201.78500366210938,
        556.9999389648438,
        220.3253936767578,
        565.8467407226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "θ",
      "bbox": [
        209.05101013183594,
        565.5771484375,
        212.84475708007812,
        571.7698974609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epdata(x) log pθ(x) ⇔min",
      "bbox": [
        221.9870147705078,
        556.4420776367188,
        324.0429382324219,
        567.7849731445312
      ],
      "direction": [
